 No JavaScript framework or build process is required. PHP routes live in the project root and `pages/`; `actions/` handles forms, `api/` handles JSON, and `app/` holds authentication, database access, weather processing and analysis.
 
+## Simple PHP and PDO organization
+
+The code uses the course pattern: a constructor receives one PDO connection, and each class has ordinary methods with prepared SQL statements.
+
+| File | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `app/config.php` | Small settings array and shared `db()` connection helper |
+| `app/Database.php` | `Database::connect()` opens and reuses PDO |
+| `app/environment.php` | Loads existing private `.env` settings |
+| `app/paths.php` | Local root and browser URL base, including Herd/XAMPP detection |
+| `app/classes/User.php` | Create resident accounts |
+| `app/classes/Location.php` | Find, create and deactivate locations |
+| `app/classes/Reading.php` | Read, save, archive and correct readings |
+| `app/classes/Report.php` | Submit, list, review and delete reports |
+| `app/repositories.php` | Short compatibility functions called by existing pages |
+| `app/geography.php` | Checks whether coordinates are inside Irisan |
+| `app/csv.php` | CSV downloads, verification, parsing and transactional location import |
+
+PHP includes use `__DIR__`; links, assets and form actions use `url()`. Keep your existing `.env`: no database migration or setting changes are needed for this refactor. Keep `.htaccess` for Apache protection. Location imports still require an unchanged signed Locations export from the same installation; reading and report CSVs are downloads only.
+
 ## Main features
 
 - Resident registration/login, an Irisan map, saved reading history and a manually triggered weather refresh.
